{"results":[{"url":"https://intelligentias.in/eligibility-criteria-for-upsc-civil-services-examination-cse/","final_url":"https://intelligentias.in/eligibility-criteria-for-upsc-civil-services-examination-cse/","title":"Eligibility Criteria for UPSC Civil Services Examination (CSE) – Intelligent IAS","description":null,"language":"en","text":"Check UPSC Eligibility\n\n## UPSC Eligibility Checker & Planner\n\nQuick evaluation: Age, Attempts, Physical standards & Exam roadmaps.\n\nTarget Examination Stream:\n\nCivil Services (CSE)\n\n Forest Service (IFoS)\n\n Both Exams\n\nDate of Birth:\n\nCategory:\n\nGeneral / EWS\nOBC\nSC / ST\nPwBD (Persons with Benchmark Disabilities)\n\nSpecial Relaxation Group:\n\nNone\nEx-Servicemen (Commissioned Officers / ECOs / SSCOs)\nDomiciled in J&K during Jan 1, 1980 to Dec 31, 1989\n\nEducational Status:\n\nGraduate / Final Year\nUndergraduate\n\nPrevious Attempts:\nℹ️ Rules?\n\n💡 **Official Rule:** Simply applying and getting an admit card does *not* count. An attempt is counted only if you actually sat for at least one paper (GS Paper-I) in the Prelims exam.\n\n**IFoS Degree Requirement:** Do you hold a Bachelor's degree with Animal Husbandry, Botany, Chemistry, Geology, Mathematics, Physics, Statistics, Zoology, or Agriculture/Forestry/Engineering?\n\nCheck Physical Standards for Uniformed Services (IPS)\n\nGender:\n\nMale\nFemale\n\nHeight (in cm):\n\nWant to read detailed rules? \n\nRead Official Guide →\n\nThe **Union Public Service Commission (UPSC)** conducts the **Civil Services Examination (CSE)** every year to recruit officers for prestigious services such as the **Indian Administrative Service (IAS), Indian Police Service (IPS), Indian Foreign Service (IFS), Indian Revenue Service (IRS)**, and several other Central Civil Services.\n\nBefore starting your preparation, it is essential to understand the **eligibility criteria** prescribed by UPSC. The eligibility conditions primarily relate to **Nationality, Educational Qualification, Age Limit, Number of Attempts, and Physical Standards**.\n\nThis article provides a comprehensive overview of the UPSC CSE eligibility criteria.\n\n#### **1. Nationality**\n\nThe nationality requirements vary depending on the service for which a candidate is applying.\n\nFor Indian Administrative Service (IAS), Indian Police Service (IPS) and Indian Foreign Service (IFS)\n\nThe candidate **must be a citizen of India.**\n\nFor Other Services\n\nA candidate must be either:\n\n* A citizen of India; or\n* A citizen of Nepal; or\n* A citizen of Bhutan; or\n* A Tibetan refugee who came to India before **1 January 1962** with the intention of permanently settling in India; or\n* A person of Indian origin who has migrated from Pakistan, Myanmar, Sri Lanka, Kenya, Uganda, Tanzania, Zambia, Malawi, Zaire, Ethiopia or Vietnam with the intention of permanently settling in India.\n\nCandidates belonging to categories other than Indian citizens must possess an eligibility certificate issued by the Government of India.\n\n#### 2. Educational Qualification\n\nA candidate must hold a **Bachelor’s Degree** from:\n\n* A recognized university established by an Act of Parliament or State Legislature; or\n* An institution established by an Act of Parliament; or\n* A university declared as a deemed university under the UGC Act.\n\n###### Candidates who are also eligible\n\n* Final-year students awaiting results (subject to fulfilling UPSC notification requirements before the Mains Examination).\n* Candidates possessing professional or technical qualifications recognized by the Government of India as equivalent to a degree.\n* Candidates who have passed MBBS but have not completed internship may also be eligible subject to UPSC conditions.\n\n##### Is there any minimum percentage?\n\n**No.**\n\nUPSC does **not prescribe any minimum percentage or CGPA**.\n\nWhether you have scored **45%, 60%, 75%, or 90%**, you are equally eligible, provided you possess a recognized bachelor’s degree.\n\n#### 3. Age Limit\n\nThe age is calculated as on the date mentioned in the UPSC notification (generally **1st August** of the examination year).\n\n##### General Category (UR/EWS)\n\n* Minimum Age: **21 years**\n* Maximum Age: **32 years**\n\n---\n\n##### Age Relaxation\n\n| Category | Maximum Age |\n| --- | --- |\n| General / EWS | 32 years |\n| OBC | 35 years |\n| SC/ST | 37 years |\n| PwBD | Up to 42 years (depending on category) |\n| Ex-Servicemen | As per UPSC Rules |\n\nCandidates are advised to refer to the latest UPSC notification for detailed relaxation provisions applicable to specific categories.\n\n#### 4. Number of Attempts\n\nEvery appearance in the Preliminary Examination counts as one attempt.\n\n| Category | Number of Attempts |\n| --- | --- |\n| General | 6 |\n| EWS | 6 |\n| OBC | 9 |\n| SC/ST | Unlimited (up to the maximum age limit) |\n| PwBD | As per applicable UPSC rules |\n\n##### Important Note\n\nMerely filling the application form does **not** count as an attempt.\n\nAn attempt is counted only if the candidate actually appears in at least one paper of the Preliminary Examination.","author":null,"published_date":"2026-07-24T08:35:04+00:00","latency_ms":5738.916140999208,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}